$ and $Q(x,y)=x.$ Determine the missing part of the equation." :question/worked-solution "Our simple, smooth, closed path $C$ is positively oriented, and  \n\n$$\n\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=1-0=1.\n$$\n\nSo, according to Green's theorem, we can write the area of the region $D$ enclosed by the curve $C$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Area}(D) & ={∬}_{D}\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y})\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∮}_{C}P\\,\\text{d}x+Q\\,\\text{d}y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n  \n\nSubstituting $P(x,y)=0$ and $Q(x,y)=x,$ we get\n\n$$\n{∮}_{C}P\\,\\text{d}x+Q\\,\\text{d}y={∮}_{C}x\\,\\text{d}y.\n$$\n\n \n\nThe derivative of $r(t)$ is\n\n$$\n{r}^{′}(t)=⟨-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t⟩.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write our line integral as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∮}_{C}x\\,dy & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\cdot 3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,dt \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }9{cos}^{2}⁡t\\,dt.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186511584 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "8644454b-ee25-59fd-ae65-9770a0b44442" :knowledge-point/title "Expressing the Area Bounded by a Closed Curve Using Green’s Theorem"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "65573630-2003-5f37-a3a0-d25c98f4401a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3(3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-\\operatorname{cos}⁡3t)(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-\\operatorname{cos}⁡3t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186510996} {:answer/id #uuid "6e780ffa-2a00-5af3-b5f3-92f795812999" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3(3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+\\operatorname{cos}⁡3t)(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-\\operatorname{cos}⁡3t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186511012} {:answer/id #uuid "9dbf5317-be7f-5ed0-a334-2b540864d0af" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3(\\operatorname{sin}⁡t-\\operatorname{sin}⁡3t)(3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡3t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186511112} {:answer/id #uuid "a54848