}A \\\\  & ={∮}_{C}P\\,\\text{d}x+Q\\,\\text{d}y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n  \n\nSubstituting $P(x,y)=0$ and $Q(x,y)=x,$ we get\n\n$$\n{∮}_{C}P\\,\\text{d}x+Q\\,\\text{d}y={∮}_{C}x\\,\\text{d}y.\n$$\n\n \n\nThe derivative of $r(t)$ is\n\n$$\n{r}^{′}(t)=⟨-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+3\\operatorname{sin}⁡3t,\\,3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-3\\operatorname{cos}⁡3t⟩.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write our line integral as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∮}_{C}x\\,dy & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }(3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-\\operatorname{cos}⁡3t)\\cdot (3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-3\\operatorname{cos}⁡3t)\\,dt \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }3(3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-\\operatorname{cos}⁡3t)(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-\\operatorname{cos}⁡3t)\\,dt.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] :knowledge-point/title "Expressing the Area Bounded by a Closed Curve Using Green’s Theorem"}]}
